      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the cost, insurance, and freight of the goods to the destination port in Germany. However, the risk of loss or damage to the goods transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods are loaded onto the vessel at the port of shipment in Korea. So, in your electronics contract, the seller will cover the shipping costs, insurance, and freight until the goods are loaded onto the ship, but from that moment on, the buyer bears the risk. It's like the seller is the one who takes care of the goods until they leave the Korean port, but once they leave, it's the buyer's responsibility to watch out for them. Just remember, the seller is like the trusty guardian of the goods until they hit the water, after which it's up to the buyer to keep an eye on them.",
